From 9e60ab8bab35e703aa6e5f7153969b0e80c9ac77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tigerblue77 <37409593+tigerblue77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:01:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Linux: leave unfilled pages to their filler in update_pages()

update_pages() copies only the bytes a write covered into each cached
page and then marks the page up to date.  For a page that was never
filled, the rest of the page is whatever the allocator left there, and
it becomes visible to mmap and to mappedread().

Such pages exist.  zfs_getpage() unlocks its page while it waits for
the range lock, so a writer holding that lock can reach the page before
it is filled, and other readers can see it after the writer is done and
before zfs_getpage() relocks it.  Readahead that stops early also
leaves its unconsumed pages cached and not up to date on kernels before
6.14, whose read_pages() removes only the async part of the window.

Skip a page that is neither up to date nor dirty.  Every filler
(zfs_getpage(), mappedread(), readahead) takes the range lock, which
our callers hold as writer, so the filler reads this write from the
DMU once it is done.  This is also needed before readahead may stop
early on range lock contention.

Signed-off-by: Tigerblue77 <37409593+tigerblue77@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 module/os/linux/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/os/linux/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c b/module/os/linux/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c
index cb6321e..3ba997b 100644
--- a/module/os/linux/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c
+++ b/module/os/linux/zfs/zfs_vnops_os.c
@@ -249,6 +249,17 @@ update_pages(znode_t *zp, int64_t start, int len, objset_t *os)
 		uint64_t nbytes = MIN(PAGE_SIZE - off, len);
 
 		struct page *pp = find_lock_page(mp, start >> PAGE_SHIFT);
+		if (pp != NULL && !PageUptodate(pp) && !PageDirty(pp)) {
+			/*
+			 * Nobody has filled this page yet.  Copying in only
+			 * the bytes written here would mark the rest of it up
+			 * to date.  Its filler needs the range lock our caller
+			 * holds as writer, so it will read this data instead.
+			 */
+			unlock_page(pp);
+			put_page(pp);
+			pp = NULL;
+		}
 		if (pp) {
 			if (mapping_writably_mapped(mp))
 				flush_dcache_page(pp);
-- 
2.56.0

